## LEARNINGS
- Touch events conflict with browser navigation/scroll on mobile — canvas panning must stand down while the user is scrolling; be careful with preventDefault in useCanvasEvents.
- All navigation flows through updateCurrentSection in useSectionManagement — the single integration point for any tracking or navigation feature.
- Voice is the product: specific first-person copy ("Tall skinny fat, slight athletic", the Now section) is what works; template phrasing reads as Lovable boilerplate. Full critiques: dev/research/23May26_claude_idea.md and 23May26_gemini_ideas.txt.
- Axis mental model for future sections: professional content on the horizontal axis, personal on the vertical. Don't rearrange existing sections; apply when adding new ones.
- Section Registry Single Source of Truth: All sections are registered canonically in `src/data/sections.ts` (`SECTIONS` array). React Router (`AppRoutes.tsx`), navigation validation (`InfiniteCanvas.tsx`), breadcrumbs (`NavigationBreadcrumb.tsx`), SEO metadata (`SEO.tsx`), and SSG prerendering (`scripts/prerender.js`) automatically consume this single registry. To add a new section, define it in `src/data/sections.ts` and add its component to `SectionRenderer.tsx`.
- Heading hierarchy on 2D infinite canvas: pass `isActive` to section components so only the active section renders `<h1>`, preventing crawler penalties for multiple concurrent `<h1>` headings on the un-unmounted canvas tree.
- Static Site Pre-rendering (SSG): `scripts/prerender.js` runs automatically in `npm run postbuild` via Puppeteer, rendering full static HTML files for all section routes and sub-routes (`dist/work/index.html`, etc.) so Bingbot and Googlebot receive full `<h1>` headers and `200 OK` static HTML on initial HTTP GET.

